	<h2>22. World War II</h2>
	<div class="content-content">





<figure class="wp-block-image alignwide size-large"><img fetchpriority="high" decoding="async" width="1024" height="512" src="https://www.americanyawp.com/textbook/wp-content/uploads/2014/02/Picture1-1024x512.jpg" alt="A soldier on a beach stares off camera." class="wp-image-470" srcset="https://www.americanyawp.com/textbook/wp-content/uploads/2014/02/Picture1-1024x512.jpg 1024w, https://www.americanyawp.com/textbook/wp-content/uploads/2014/02/Picture1-300x150.jpg 300w, https://www.americanyawp.com/textbook/wp-content/uploads/2014/02/Picture1-768x384.jpg 768w, https://www.americanyawp.com/textbook/wp-content/uploads/2014/02/Picture1-1536x768.jpg 1536w, https://www.americanyawp.com/textbook/wp-content/uploads/2014/02/Picture1.jpg 1600w" sizes="(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px" /><figcaption class="wp-element-caption">Walter Rosenblum, &#8220;D Day Rescue, Omaha Beach,&#8221; via <a href="http://www.loc.gov/pictures/item/2004681507/">Library of Congress</a>.</figcaption></figure>







